# Files that are consumed by Linux (inside the dev container, or by Docker at
# build time) must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows, where
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite them to CRLF. A CRLF shebang makes
# the kernel fail the script with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and CRLF in a
# Dockerfile breaks the trailing-backslash line continuations.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
